{"type":"text","timestamp":1787403121477,"sessionID":"ses_fd67a84a8ffehrOOHRAoW0cThP","part":{"id":"prt_029872a5d001Vw7u8G1kTuTuk4","messageID":"msg_02986fb080017oX34bc2Xeb7lx","sessionID":"ses_fd67a84a8ffehrOOHRAoW0cThP","type":"text","text":"All the requirement-specified cases pass. The one \"FAIL\" was my own incorrect test expectation: `diff('1.0.0','1.0.0-1')` returning `'major'` is actually **order-independent and consistent** with the stepping-out rule (both orderings yield `'major'`), which matches the requirement that results don't depend on argument order.\n\nSummary of the fix in `functions/diff.js`:\n- `compare === 0` (identical, or build-metadata-only difference) → `null`.\n- Both prereleases: `premajor`/`preminor`/`prepatch` by main diff, else `prerelease`.\n- Stepping **out** of a prerelease: `major` when minor==patch==0, `minor` when minor!=0 && patch==0, else `patch`.\n- Stepping **into** a prerelease: `premajor`/`preminor`/`prepatch` by main diff, else `prerelease`.\n- Both releases: `major`/`minor`/`patch`.\n- Invalid input: `parse(..., true)` throws `TypeError`.","time":{"start":1787403119197,"end":1787403121472}}}
